
🏍️ Overview
Grand-Opening is a multi‑page retail website for motorcycle gear, built as part of the ECPI SDC260 course project.
The site includes product listings, dynamic cart functionality, checkout flow, brand pages, gear guides, and a fully functional Network Connection Test page required for Phase 5.5.

The project is designed to run both locally (for telemetry testing) and through GitHub Pages for deployment.

🚀 Current Website Features
🛒 Shopping & Product Pages
All product pages are fully implemented and organized under the /shop-*.html structure:

Helmets (shop-helmets.html)

Jackets (shop-jackets.html)

Gloves (shop-gloves.html)

Boots (shop-boots.html)

Pants (shop-pants.html)

Accessories (shop-accessories.html)

Women’s Gear (shop-women.html)

Sale Items (shop-sale.html)

General Shop Page (shop.html)

Each page uses:

ProductDisplay.js — dynamically loads product cards

cart.js — handles cart interactions

🛒 Shopping Cart System
Implemented features include:

Add‑to‑cart buttons across all product pages

Dynamic cart listing (cart.html)

Item quantity handling

Price display

Cart persistence during session

💳 Checkout & Order Confirmation
Checkout form (checkout.html)

Order confirmation page (order-confirmation.html)

Improved readability and structure

Form validation and user flow

🧭 Navigation & Informational Pages
Homepage (index.html)

Brands (brands.html)

Gear Guide (gear-guide.html)

About (about.html)

Support (support.html)

All pages use consistent header, footer, and styling.

🌐 Network Connection Test Page (New for 5.5)
File: network-test.html  
Script: network-test.js

This page dynamically displays telemetry when the site is run locally:

Local Host Name

Current Communication Port

Current Transmission Protocol

Last Time Launched

Telemetry updates automatically using JavaScript:

javascript
window.location.hostname
window.location.port
window.location.protocol
new Date().toLocaleString()
This satisfies the “Dynamically Updated Telemetrics” requirement in the rubric.

